  ],
  "opener_md": "# ReviewLens \u00b7 Competitive Diagnosis\n\n**No cross-company difference clears the significance bar in this sample. The loudest pain by raw rate is support (28.6 per-100, n=16), reported for orientation only.**\n\nAn LLM agent read 4011 public reviews across USim and 5 competitors over the last 12 months, classified each into a pain taxonomy, and benchmarked rates per-100-reviews with 95% confidence intervals.\n\n## Top-3 Pains\n\n| Pain | USim per-100 (95% CI) | Field median per-100 | Delta | Evidence |\n|------|----------------------|---------------------|-------|----------|\n| Positive (Positive) | 42.9 (30.8\u201355.9) | 33.0 | +30.3 vs Jetpac | [Directional] |\n| Support (Negative) | 28.6 (18.4\u201341.5) | 8.4 | +27.6 vs Jetpac | [Directional] |\n| Coverage Speed (Negative) | 8.9 (3.9\u201319.3) | 13.4 | -21.8 vs Saily | [Directional] |\n\n## Competitive Read\n\nOn support (negative), USim trends higher than Jetpac (n=16; small sample \u2014 treat as indicative only) [Directional].  \nOn coverage speed (negative), USim trends lower than Saily (n=5; small sample \u2014 treat as indicative only) [Directional].  \nOn refund billing (negative), USim trends lower than Saily (n=1; small sample \u2014 treat as indicative only) [Directional].\n\n## Month-One Interventions\n\n- Set a 4-hour first-response SLA; auto-triage tickets by theme (activation, refund) and route to a specialist queue \u2014 remove the silence that turns a resolvable issue into a one-star review.\n- Publish a real-time coverage map with honest speed tiers per country; set expectations before purchase to reduce coverage-related disappointment and the 1-star reviews that follow.\n- Assign the top-ranked pain an owner, a 30-day target metric, and a weekly review cadence \u2014 the data is diagnostic; the fix requires an execution owner.\n\n---\n\n*Sample: 4011 reviews (appstore: 4011); recency window 12 months; competitors benchmarked: Airalo, Holafly, Jetpac, Nomad, Saily. All rates per-100 reviews with 95% Wilson CIs. Supported = both samples \u2265 n-floor AND CIs non-overlapping; Directional = otherwise (thin sample or overlapping intervals).*\n"
}